Add a minimal browser firmware-upload UI on top of the POST
/api/ota endpoint from patch 0016. Applied only to nanoc6-wifi
and atoms3-lite-wifi via variants.json; nanoc6-thread never
applies, compiles, links, or exposes any of the code here.

Scope, kept minimal (no new C++ handler or endpoint, no
multipart, no XHR / progress bar, no polling / reconnect loop,
no authentication, no settings or log changes, no new runtime
dependency, no partition change, no build-file change, no
other UI redesign):

  * MODIFY main/aliro_local_web.cpp -> kIndexHtml only:
      - New "Update firmware" section between the Recent logs
        block and the Machine endpoints list:
          * <p><small> warning that the .bin must match the
            board and transport variant.
          * <form id="ota-form" onsubmit="return false">
            containing a required <input type="file"
            id="ota-file" accept=".bin"> and a
            <button type="submit" id="ota-submit">
            Upload and restart</button>.
          * <p id="ota-status" role="status"
            aria-live="polite">.
      - /api/ota added to the Machine endpoints <ul>: a plain
        <code>POST /api/ota</code> item documenting the
        application/octet-stream body and the exact
        {"ok":true,"restarting":true} success response.
      - New <script> IIFE, SEPARATE from the QR IIFE, the
        settings IIFE, and the log-viewer IIFE, wires the OTA
        form. On submit:
          * preventDefault so the browser never navigates.
          * Read the selected File. Missing or zero-byte file
            -> setStatus red, controls stay enabled, return.
          * Disable the file input and the submit button; set
            status to Uploading (aria-live).
          * fetch POST /api/ota with headers
            'Content-Type':'application/octet-stream' and the
            File as the raw body. No multipart, no FormData,
            no manual chunking, no progress bar.
          * On the response: require r.ok, else throw
            'HTTP <status>'; then call r.json() (letting
            r.json() reject with its original error name so
            SyntaxError / TypeError are classified correctly);
            then require the strict schema
            j.ok === true && j.restarting === true, else throw
            'unexpected response'.
          * On success: setStatus 'Update accepted. The device
            is restarting.' Controls STAY DISABLED so a false
            success cannot be re-submitted while the device
            reboots.
          * On any failure (HTTP, network, JSON, schema, body
            read): setStatus red with the failure message,
            RE-ENABLE both controls so the user can retry.

Explicit non-goals for this patch: no new C++ handler or
endpoint (POST /api/ota is patch 0016), no multipart parser,
no XHR / XMLHttpRequest, no upload progress bar, no polling or
reconnect loop, no auth, no settings or log changes, no new
runtime dependency, no partition change, no build-system
change (SRC_DIRS "." already picks up main/ .cpp files), no
other UI redesign.

